Q: AngularJS uncheck radio button A: <p>Look at the <a href="https://docs.angularjs.org/api/ng/input/input%5Bradio%5D#!" rel="nofollow noreferrer">documentation</a></p>

<pre><code>&lt;div class="inline-group"&gt;
        &lt;label class="radio"&gt;
            &lt;input type="radio" name="stage{{$index}}" ng-model="item.Stage" value="true"&gt;
            &lt;i&gt;&lt;/i&gt; Started
        &lt;/label&gt;
        &lt;label class="radio"&gt;
            &lt;input type="radio" name="stage{{$index}}" ng-model="item.Stage" value="false"&gt;
            &lt;i&gt;&lt;/i&gt; Completed
        &lt;/label&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
</code></pre>

<p>And for a true / false selection, use a check box instead of a radio buttton</p>

<p><strong>Updated</strong></p>

<p>With an enum, in your scope:</p>

<pre><code>$scope.stageEnum = { Started: 0, Completed: 1 };
</code></pre>

<p>your view :</p>

<pre><code>&lt;div class="inline-group"&gt;
            &lt;label class="radio"&gt;
                &lt;input type="radio" name="stage{{$index}}" ng-model="item.Stage" value="stageEnum.Started"&gt;
                &lt;i&gt;&lt;/i&gt; Started
            &lt;/label&gt;
            &lt;label class="radio"&gt;
                &lt;input type="radio" name="stage{{$index}}" ng-model="item.Stage" value="stageEnum.Completed"&gt;
                &lt;i&gt;&lt;/i&gt; Completed
            &lt;/label&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
</code></pre>
